I had this problem too but I think I have solved it.  (This
is empirical, not proved via source diving).

I have found that by trying to move into the ghoul will get
it to move in this situation.  You can't displace it while in
the shop, but moving into it will make it move in the following
turn.  I  think this is to prevent the ghoul from trapping you
in the shop by sitting in the doorway and fighting the
shopkeeper forever.

So this behavior allows you to "herd" a ghoul out of
a shop by encouraging it to move until it gets into the
doorway, in which case you interpose yourself between the
ghoul and shop and herd the ghoul away until he loses
interest in the shopkeeper.  Seems to work for me.

